he $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$ is $\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\text{{}{h}_{1},{h}_{3}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H).$"] [:db/cas 17592186484820 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186484855 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186484909 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186484913 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186484941 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186484953 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}40 & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 25 & 1 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}40 & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 25 & 1 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & 1 & 15\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186484957 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186484962 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 & 5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 5 & 15 \\\\ -10\\sqrt{7} & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 5 & 5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 5 & 15 \\\\ -10\\sqrt{7} & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186485049 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 6 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 3\\sqrt{5}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 6 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6 & 